  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given a string SSS, find the longest substring that is a palindrome. A palindrome is a string that reads the same forwards and backwards. If multiple palindromic substrings have the same length, return the one that appears first in the string.\n\nFor example, if S=\"aaaabbaa\"S = \\text{\"aaaabbaa\"}S=\"aaaabbaa\", the longest palindromic substring is \"aabbaa\"\\text{\"aabbaa\"}\"aabbaa\".\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line contains NNN - length of the string\nSecond line contains the string SSS\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nPrint the longest palindromic substring\nIf multiple solutions exist, print the leftmost one",
    "constraints": [
      "1 ≤ N ≤ 10^3"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
